 "method": "tests/e2e/specs/inquiry-states.spec.ts on the review instance (live snapshot, Chromium, one worker). Every record is made through WP-CLI inside the one test that reads it and deleted with it; the fixture's status-notification hooks are removed for the fixture request alone, so no mail job is queued for an inquiry nobody sent. The leak assertion reads the whole document element (not the rendered text), so hidden markup counts; the order key is asserted absent only in the cases that never carried one, because a visitor who supplies it sees it echoed inside the verification and sign-in forms' own fields. The 390 fit check walks every page of each 390 test.",
 "observations": {
  "signed_in_summary": "A signed-in customer whose billing name, email and company are stored reads one closed <details> row 'Your reply details / Ihre Kontaktdaten' carrying 'Maria Beispiel · <email>' and 'Change / Ändern'; the field block is hidden, the message field and the send button stay open, and the guest-only consent line and guest box are absent. Opening the row shows the stored name, email and company prefilled. This is the owner ruling of 2026-10-17 (a signed-in customer's details fold into one row), not the guest form.",
  "confirmation_key": "The confirmation link carries WooCommerce's order key. A wrong key, a missing key and an order id that does not exist all answer the recovery notice and no inquiry data (owner, company, product, key). A correct key still needs the owner: an anonymous visitor meets WooCommerce's own gate — email verification for a guest inquiry, the sign-in form for a customer-owned one — with the recovery notice hidden by the storefront sheet (it is display:none whenever the order wrapper is absent), and another signed-in customer reads the same gate notice without a login form, because WooCommerce's global/form-login.php returns for any signed-in user. The owner, and the owner of an inquiry backdated by 400 days, open the confirmation with the custom success card, the one-business-day promise and the product; no payment-method line appears.",
  "grace_period": "WooCommerce skips the email-verification step within ten minutes of an order (woocommerce_order_email_verification_grace_period); the guest fixture is therefore an hour old, which is what opening an emailed link means. Keys do not expire: they are the order key, so the backdated inquiry opens for its owner exactly like a fresh one."
 },
 "scope_boundary": "Local review instance, Chromium only, EN and DE at 1440 and 390. Does not prove touch devices beyond the 390 emulation, mail delivery, or the verification-code round trip a visitor would complete from the gate.",
 "run": "8 passed (2.1m), review instance, 2026-11-11; PR #1072 check success on fcfe5db3",
 "boundary_confirmation": "Re-run after the folded-state 390 fit check was added: all eight shapes green again. PR #1072 CI (check) passed on the final commit."
